%erg 0.1
Title: Make install-erg-binary staleness check asset-aware
Created: 2026-05-29
Author: haduong

--- log ---
2026-05-29T19:33Z haduong created

--- body ---
## Context
PR #183 (ticket 0165) fixed the CI `rebuild-binary.yml` path filter so that
changes to `//go:embed` assets under `src/go/assets/` trigger a rebuild of the
committed bootstrap binary. The same bug class survives one layer down, in the
local install path.

`Makefile:108` (`install-erg-binary`) decides whether the committed bootstrap
binary is fresh enough to install by running:

    find src/go -name '*.go' -newer "$(BOOTSTRAP_BIN)"

This only detects changes to `.go` source files. If a developer edits an
embedded asset under `src/go/assets/` (which the binary bakes in via
`//go:embed`) without touching any `.go` file, the staleness check sees no
newer source, treats the committed binary as fresh, and installs a stale
binary — exactly the 0160 corruption-shipping failure mode, but on the local
`make install-erg-binary` path instead of CI.

## Relevant files
- `Makefile` (line ~108, `install-erg-binary` target) — the asset-blind staleness check

## Actions
1. Broaden the staleness probe so it also detects newer embedded assets.
   Mirror the #183 fix intent (`src/go/**`): probe all tracked inputs the
   binary embeds, e.g. `find src/go -type f -newer "$(BOOTSTRAP_BIN)"`, or
   scope to `-name '*.go' -o -path 'src/go/assets/*'`. Avoid false positives
   from regenerable/non-embedded files if `-type f` is too broad.
2. Keep the existing platform guard (`Linux`/`x86_64`/binary-present) intact.

## Test
- Add a Makefile/shell test (parallel to the rebuild-binary asset test) that:
  touches an asset under `src/go/assets/` to be newer than the committed
  binary, runs the `install-erg-binary` decision logic, and asserts it falls
  through to the `go build` branch rather than installing the stale binary.

## Verification
- [ ] Editing only a `src/go/assets/*` file marks the committed binary stale
- [ ] Editing only a `src/go/*.go` file still marks it stale (no regression)
- [ ] An untouched tree still installs the committed binary (no spurious rebuild)
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants
- The offline/no-Go fallback behavior is unchanged: when assets are fresh and
  the platform matches, the committed binary is still installed without Go.

## Exit criteria
- `install-erg-binary` rebuilds (or refuses the stale binary) when any embedded
  input — `.go` source OR `src/go/assets/*` — is newer than the committed
  bootstrap binary, covered by a test.
